# Markdown format (agent knowledge)

MarkSpace notes use a **dialect** of Markdown (wiki-links, Draw.io embeds, image widths, colored HTML tables, etc.). The built-in chat agent learns this from [`docs/markdown-format.md`](docs/markdown-format.md).

## Single source of truth

- Spec: `docs/markdown-format.md`
- Core rules (Ask system prompt, plus IELTS and lexicon writers) live between `<!-- core-rules:start -->` and `<!-- core-rules:end -->`.
- The full guide is inlined into the Agent system prompt and into the `edit_notes` and `media` specialist prompts (`MARKDOWN_FORMAT_GUIDE` in `src/ai/markdownFormat.ts`).

## When you change the format

If you change on-disk syntax or round-trip behavior in any of these areas, **update `docs/markdown-format.md` in the same change** (including the core-rules block when the change is agent-critical):

- `src/lib/wikiMarkdown.ts` — wiki-links, `![[*.drawio]]` embeds
- `src/lib/hashtagMarkdown.ts` — inline `#tags` ↔ Live intermediate HTML
- `src/lib/imageMarkdown.ts` — `![alt|width](…)` / assets
- `src/lib/tableMarkdown.ts` — colored table HTML
- `src/lib/normalizeMarkdown.ts` — CRLF / fence healing
- `src/editor/schema.ts` and `src/editor/{mermaid,plantuml,drawio}/` — custom blocks
- `src/editor/tag/` — Live hashtag decorations / `#` suggestions
- `src/editor/NoteEditor.tsx` — load/save pipeline that affects on-disk markdown

Otherwise the in-app agent will keep writing obsolete or unsupported syntax.

Keep product UI copy in English; this rule is for developers and coding agents working on MarkSpace itself.
